# Close Enough — environment configuration
#
# There is almost nothing to configure. The Cloudflare Worker serves the game
# client and the multiplayer backend from one origin, so there are no URLs to
# wire together, no CORS to configure, and no secrets anywhere.
#
# Copy to `.env` only if you want a local override. An empty file — or no file
# at all — is a valid configuration for both local play and production.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client (apps/web) — must be prefixed VITE_ to reach the browser
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the browser should open its game socket.
#
# Leave EMPTY (the default) for same-origin, which is correct for:
#   - local development (Vite proxies /ws and /api to wrangler)
#   - the one-click launcher (the Worker serves the client itself)
#   - production on Cloudflare (same — one Worker, one origin)
#
# Set it only if you host the frontend somewhere other than the Worker, in
# which case point it at the Worker's public URL.
# Example: VITE_SERVER_URL=https://close-enough.your-subdomain.workers.dev
# VITE_SERVER_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Port the Vite dev server proxies its /ws and /api traffic to. Only change
# this if you also pass a matching --port to wrangler.
# Default: 8787
# SERVER_PORT=8787

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional accounts (Google sign-in)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These are NOT read from this file. They are Worker configuration and live in
# `apps/worker/.dev.vars` locally (see .dev.vars.example) and in wrangler vars
# plus `wrangler secret put` in production:
#
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID      public   -> apps/worker/wrangler.toml [vars]
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET  secret   -> npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
#   SESSION_SECRET        secret   -> npx wrangler secret put SESSION_SECRET
#
# With none of them set, the game runs exactly as it always has and simply
# does not offer signing in. Accounts are optional in every sense.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `npm run deploy` uses your Cloudflare login from `wrangler login`, which is
# stored by wrangler outside this repository. There is no API token to place
# in a file here, and none should ever be committed.
#
# Durable Object bindings and the Worker name live in apps/worker/wrangler.toml
# rather than in environment variables, because they are part of the
# application's shape rather than its configuration.
